{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1521"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge science/maths","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/science__maths.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",958],["+","It works for solids that are not Platonic too: a square pyramid, the shape of Giza, has 5 faces (a square base and four triangles), 5 vertices and 8 edges – four around the base and four rising to the apex – and 5 − 8 + 5 is again 2. "],["=",67]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",932],["+","Sie gilt auch für Körper, die nicht platonisch sind: Eine quadratische Pyramide, die Form von Gizeh, hat 5 Flächen (eine quadratische Grundfläche und vier Dreiecke), 5 Ecken und 8 Kanten – vier rund um die Grundfläche und vier, die zur Spitze aufsteigen –, und 5 − 8 + 5 ergibt wieder 2. "],["=",55]]}]},
